+# Privacy by Design: The Daily Grind website
+
+This document records how the public site handles personal data, and the rules
+contributors must follow. `npm run audit:privacy` enforces most of these rules
+automatically. Run it before every deploy.
+
+## Principles
+
+| Principle | How it is applied |
+| --- | --- |
+| **Data minimisation** | The site collects nothing beyond what the sign-in session needs. Only web-storage keys on the allow-list in `public/js/privacy.js` may exist; any other key is deleted on page load. Stored choices hold no identifiers, keep the save date only to the day, and expire after 180 days. Images have their EXIF/GPS/XMP metadata stripped. |
+| **Privacy as the default** | Every optional purpose (for example analytics) is **off** until the visitor opts in. Global Privacy Control and Do Not Track are honoured as an opt-out the page can't override. `/.well-known/gpc.json` declares GPC support. |
+| **No third parties** | All assets (CSS, JS, images, favicon) are self-hosted. The site uses no CDNs, web fonts, analytics, tag managers, social widgets or embeds. Any third party must first be reviewed and added to `third-parties.json`. |
+| **Secure handling** | Strict CSP (`default-src 'none'`, no inline code, Trusted Types), `Referrer-Policy: same-origin`, a restrictive `Permissions-Policy`, HSTS, COOP/COEP/CORP, and `no-store` on HTML. Logout is a POST, and the backend should answer it with `Clear-Site-Data`. |
+| **User control** | The "Privacy Choices" link in the footer lets visitors view and change consent and wipe everything the site stored in their browser. |
+
+## Data inventory (client side)
+
+| Storage | Key / name | Purpose | Contents | Lifetime |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `localStorage` | `dg_privacy_v1` | Remember privacy choices | `{v, savedOn: "YYYY-MM-DD", consents: {analytics: bool}}` | 180 days, or until cleared |
+| Cookie (set by backend) | session cookie | Sign-in | Opaque session ID. Must be `HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax` | Session |
+
+To add a new key, put it on the `ALLOWED_STORAGE_KEYS` allow-list **and** in this table.
+Without both, it will be deleted.
+
+## Third-party audit
+
+Current status: **no third-party origins** (checked by `npm run audit:privacy`).
+
+| Date | Change |
+| --- | --- |
+| 2026-11-04 | Removed `images.unsplash.com`: the hero image was hotlinked, which sent every visitor's IP, User-Agent and Referer to Unsplash/imgix. It is now self-hosted (`public/images/hero-*.jpg`, Unsplash License, metadata stripped). |
+
+### Adding a third party
+
+1. Ask whether it is truly needed, and whether it can be self-hosted instead.
+2. Record what personal data it receives (IP address counts) and the legal basis, and sign a DPA.
+3. Add an entry to `third-parties.json` with: `host, vendor, purpose, dataShared, legalBasis, dpaSigned, reviewedOn`.
+4. Allow the host in the matching CSP directive in `security-headers.mjs` (and the fallback `<meta>` CSP).
+5. If it is not strictly necessary, load it only when `DailyGrindPrivacy.hasConsent('<purpose>')` is true.
+6. Review every entry at least once a year. The audit fails on entries older than 365 days.
+
+## Backend requirements (outside this repo)
+
+- `POST /logout`: invalidate the session on the server and respond with the
+  `LOGOUT_HEADERS` from `security-headers.mjs` (`Clear-Site-Data: "cache", "cookies", "storage"`).
+  Protect it with a CSRF token or check the `Origin` header.
+- Session cookies: `HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax; Path=/`, with no third-party cookies.
+- Server logs: shorten IP addresses or delete them within 30 days, and never log query strings that contain personal data.
+- Send the headers from `security-headers.mjs` from any CDN or reverse proxy in front of the site.
+
+## Running locally
+
+```sh
+pnpm install
+pnpm start                # serves ./public on http://localhost:11222 with all headers
+pnpm run audit:privacy    # privacy / third-party audit (also `pnpm test`)
+```
